{
  "transcript": "[Verse 1]\nFive alarms I snooze, trying again\nDragging my feet to who knows when\nToast burned black, another late start\nFaking a smile, I play the part\n\n[Chorus]\nAmerican idle, stuck in a chair\nDreams collecting dust in dead air\nPromises sold for minimum wage\nCounting the hours in a cage\n\n[Post-Chorus]\nWhoa oh oh oh, whoa oh oh oh\nWhoa oh oh oh, American idle!\n\n[Verse 2]\nClipboard kings, they nod and yawn\nBuilding nothing as time drags on\nCoffee stains on an empty plan\nStuck on pause since change began\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nRoutine feels like a disease\nTrading fire for guarantees\n\n[Chorus]\nAmerican idle, stuck in a chair\nDreams collecting dust in dead air\nPromises sold for minimum wage\nCounting the hours in a cage\n\n[Post-Chorus]\nWhoa oh oh oh, whoa oh oh oh\nWhoa oh oh oh, American idle!\n\n",
